# README & Docs Conventions — Form Builder

## README Structure

The root README follows this exact structure. Every section must be present.

```markdown
# Form Builder

A Typeform-style form builder built with Next.js + TypeScript (frontend) and FastAPI + Python (backend), backed by PostgreSQL.

## Why This Stack

Brief paragraph (3–5 sentences) explaining the deliberate architectural choices:
- Why FastAPI over Node/Express (Pydantic type safety, async-first, auto Swagger docs, Python is natural for future ML features)
- Why Next.js App Router (React Query integration, server/client component split, Vercel-ready)
- Why JSONB for field config (schema flexibility without migrations)

## Features

- [ ] Drag-and-drop form builder with reorderable fields
- [ ] Field types: text, email, number, textarea, select, radio
- [ ] Public form view for respondents
- [ ] Response collection and dashboard
- [ ] Auto-generated API docs at `/docs`

## Data Model

Include a table or schema summary here — not just code, but a brief explanation of the key decision:

| Table         | Purpose                                      |
|---------------|----------------------------------------------|
| `forms`       | Form metadata (title, published status)      |
| `fields`      | Ordered fields with JSONB config per type    |
| `responses`   | One row per form submission                  |
| `field_answers` | One row per field answer, JSONB value      |

Key decision: `fields.config` and `field_answers.value` use JSONB to support arbitrary field types without schema changes.

## Local Setup

### Prerequisites
- Node.js 20+
- Python 3.12+
- PostgreSQL (or use the Supabase connection string from `.env`)

### Backend

\`\`\`bash
cd backend
python -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e ".[dev]"
cp .env.example .env        # fill in DATABASE_URL
uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8000
\`\`\`

API docs: http://localhost:8000/docs

### Frontend

\`\`\`bash
cd frontend
npm install
cp .env.local.example .env.local   # set NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL
npm run dev
\`\`\`

App: http://localhost:3000

### Run Tests

\`\`\`bash
cd backend
pytest tests/ -v
\`\`\`

